Revision history for Proc-ProcessTable-InfoString

0.2.0  2026-08-02/15:30
       - add proc_infostring_describe, a exportable function for
         printing what the info string means for the current OS
       - support for OpenBSD, NetBSD, DragonFly, MidnightBSD, and
         GNU/kFreeBSD
       - do not die on OSes that do not report resident memory
       - match the state case insensitively, as OpenBSD reports it
         in upper case

0.1.0  2026-07-28/21:00
       - various fixes
       - better linux support
       - a proper test

0.0.1  2019-08-28/01:55
       - Initial release.
